<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE JUNE M1 RISES 6.9 PCT ON YEAR.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE JUNE M1 RISES 6.9 PCT ON YEAR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's M1 money supply rose 6.9 percent in June year on year, the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>			  Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>			     June 97   May 97    June 96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 28.24   27.58     26.41</p>
<p>M-2			   119.09  118.91    107.70</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 147.77  147.22    134.29</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    17.73   16.96     16.45</p>
<p>Currency in active	 10.51   10.63	9.96</p>
<p>circulation</p>
